description:
systems/dream-cycle/salience-score.py's update_salience_block() regex (r'
salience:\s*
(?:[ 	]+[^
]*
)*') intended to strip the prior salience: block before appending a fresh one, but on at least one file (memory/episodic/plaud-ingest-2026-08-22-003000.md) it left an orphaned indented 'promoted: false' line dangling with no parent key just above the newly-appended clean salience: block. Corpus scan during this cycle's step-03 found the same signature (duplicate/orphaned promoted: and last-promoted-check: lines outside any salience: parent) in 289 of 291 episodic files, consistent with this bug firing incrementally across many prior nightly runs rather than being a one-off. Files remain parseable via a 'last occurrence wins' heuristic (which step-02/step-03 both rely on for now), so no promotion/scoring data was lost this cycle, but the frontmatter corruption is corpus-wide and growing by roughly one stray line per file per night.
